   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to providing that state\nlands within the Eastport-South Manor Central School District are subject to\ntaxation for school purposes",
    "basePrintNo": "S4025",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4025-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §536, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4025\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to providing that\nstate lands within the Eastport-South Manor Central School District are\nsubject to taxation for school purposes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide that state land within the Eastport-South Manor Central\nSchool District are subject to taxation for school purposes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends paragraph (e) of subdivision one of section 536 of the real prop-\nerty tax law to provide that state lands within the Eastport-South Manor\nCentral School District be subject to taxation for school purposes.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Eastport-South Manor (ESM) School District was formed in 2000 upon\nthe merger of two local districts, Eastport Union Free School District\n(UFSD) in Eastport and South Manor UFSD in Manorville. Prior to the\nmerger, the Eastport Union Free School District was receiving payments\nfor state owned lands within the district that were located within the\ncore preservation area of the Central Pine Barrens.  Because these\npayments ceased after the merger, this legislation is necessary to\nchange the name of the school district eligible for these payments from\nEastport Union Free School District to the East-South Manor Central\nSchool District in order for the payments to resume.\n\nESM is currently the most fiscally distressed school district on Long\nIsland and is facing a significant budgetary deficit. Restoration of\nthese payments would help in on-going efforts to return the district to\nfiscal stability.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020 S.5270A/A.7291A; 2018 S.8515/A.10626\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first day of April next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
